From: netdev "[PATCH net v2 3/3] net: airoha: grow the small RX rings"
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: grow the small RX rings

Staged 2026-09-01 from a netdev "[PATCH net v2 N/3]" airoha RX series (raw diff
only; author not recorded). NOT merged in torvalds/linux, stable, or OpenWrt
master as of 2026-09-01 - re-check on each master sync and drop once it lands.
Regenerated against this tree's effective airoha_eth source (0 fuzz/offset) and
cross-compiled clean (no warnings) against a built 6.18.44 on 2026-09-01.

RX_DSCP_NUM: qid 4 -> 128, default 16 -> 32 (26 of 32 rings, including
the LRO queues 24-31 from 975). Only consumer is ndesc at ring init;
page_pool pool_size stays 256.

---
diff -ruN s2/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h s3/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
@@ -41,9 +41,10 @@
 #define TX_DSCP_NUM			1024
 #define RX_DSCP_NUM(_n)			\
 	((_n) ==  2 ? 128 :		\
+	 (_n) ==  4 ? 128 :		\
 	 (_n) == 11 ? 128 :		\
 	 (_n) == 15 ? 128 :		\
-	 (_n) ==  0 ? 1024 : 16)
+	 (_n) ==  0 ? 1024 : 32)
 
 #define AIROHA_LRO_PAGE_ORDER		order_base_2(SZ_16K / PAGE_SIZE)
 #define AIROHA_MAX_NUM_LRO_QUEUES	8
